copy the\n  shell-template by hand.\n- Project structure — annotated tree showing the publishable units\n  vs. internal infrastructure (src/ ships, components/ + utils/ are\n  README stubs).\n- Local development — clone with submodules, install, dev server,\n  production builds. Notes the GitHub Packages auth requirement for\n  the consumer example.\n- Tests — unit (co-located jest), consumer smoke (against the\n  published package), and a pointer to bulma-scaffold smoke for\n  end-to-end manual verification.\n- Contributing — points at senzu/workflows/pr-workflow.md for the\n  full PR lifecycle, lists coding standards, documents the\n  tag-triggered release flow.\n\nIncludes pointers to the related repos (bulma, senzu) so readers\nlanding here from either side have a clear path through the\necosystem.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address 3 CodeRabbit findings on the README\n\n- README.md:45 — add `text` language hint to the project-tree\n  fenced block so markdown linters / GitHub''s renderer don''t treat\n  it as untyped.\n- README.md:50 — insert a blank line after the `### Prerequisites`\n  heading per markdown convention.\n- README.md:67 — fix the documented dev-server URL: webpack.config.js\n  sets `devServer.port: 3001`, so `npm run dev` lands on\n  http://localhost:3001, not :3000. Pointing contributors at the\n  correct port.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bde7ba20a276c4edb0b73eed2770e8d138e86626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/hoi-poi/git/trees/bde7ba20a276c4edb0b73eed2770e8d138e86626"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/hoi-poi/git/commits/dd5f8649ebca58888cd1f4db3e6afde44b450708","verification":{"payload":"tree bde7ba20a276c4edb0b73eed2770e8d138e86626\nparent a5a2d6be919662367a0900ef3c21279dffdb4eeb\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777258688 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777258688 -0300\n\ndocs: write a complete README (#25)\n\n* docs: write a complete README\n\nReplaces the 2-line stub with a full README covering the five sections\nthe docs epic calls for:\n\n- Overview — what Hoi-Poi is and the three concerns it ties together\n  (component library, shell template, architecture spec). Calls out\n  bulma as the scaffolding entrypoint so users don''t copy the\n  shell-template by hand.\n- Project structure — annotated tree showing the publishable units\n  vs. internal infrastructure (src/ ships, components/ + utils/ are\n  README stubs).\n- Local development — clone with submodules, install, dev server,\n  production builds. Notes the GitHub Packages auth requirement for\n  the consumer example.\n- Tests — unit (co-located jest), consumer smoke (against the\n  published package), and a pointer to bulma-scaffold smoke for\n  end-to-end manual verification.\n- Contributing — points at senzu/workflows/pr-workflow.md for the\n  full PR lifecycle, lists coding standards, documents the\n  tag-triggered release flow.\n\nIncludes pointers to the related repos (bulma, senzu) so readers\nlanding here from either side have a clear path through the\necosystem.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: address 3 CodeRabbit findings on the README\n\n- README.md:45 — add `text` language hint to the project-tree\n  fenced block so markdown linters / GitHub''s renderer don''t treat\n  it as untyped.\n- README.md:50 — insert a blank line after the `### Prerequisites`\n  heading per markdown convention.\n- README.md:67 — fix the documented dev-server URL: webpack.config.js\n  sets `devServer.port: 3001`, so `npm run dev` lands on\n  http://localhost:3001, not :3000. Pointing contributors at the\n  correct port.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) 