rred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DjAldrinho/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DjAldrinho","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DjAldrinho/foodie-connect-admin/commits/7ecb9d303e9fd6142cb0c8b8e6319a857f472251/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-14T00:21:16Z","email":"aldray.devsoft@gmail.com","name":"Aldray Narvaez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T00:21:16Z","email":"aldray.devsoft@gmail.com","name":"Aldray Narvaez"},"message":"test(phase-11): switch from Jest to Karma for Angular 21 compatibility\n\nJest and Vitest have compatibility issues with Angular 21 (ES modules).\nKarma is the official and stable testing framework for Angular.\n\nChanges:\n- Installed Karma, Jasmine, and required dependencies\n- Created karma.conf.js with ChromeHeadless browser\n- Updated angular.json to use @angular-devkit/build-angular:karma builder\n- Updated package.json scripts to use Karma (test, test:watch, test:coverage, test:headless)\n- Updated tsconfig.spec.json to use jasmine types instead of jest\n- Created src/test.ts as Karma test entry point with proper mocks\n- Fixed base.service.spec.ts to use proper generics and type annotations\n- Created environment configuration files (development and production)\n- Kept Jest/Vitest configs for future reference when compatibility improves\n\nTesting infrastructure is now ready for Phase 11 test writing.","tree":{"sha":"9d80c532b3a4863912ddddd6218ba1c6176ddc82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DjAldrinho/foodie-connect-admin/git/trees/9d80c532b3a4863912ddddd6218ba1c6176ddc82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DjAldrinho/foodie-connect-admin/git/commits/7ecb9d303e9fd6142cb0c8b8e6319a857f472251","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64451578?v=4","events_url":"https://api