 screens and broken prop usage\n\n- All 5 screens rendered blank: NativeWind v5-preview/react-native-css\n  throws repeated \"className ''undefined'' added or removed a variable\n  after the initial render\" churn on plain react-native View/Text/\n  ScrollView/TouchableOpacity, collapsing the ScrollView''s native frame\n  to just its padding and clipping all content. Replaced className\n  styling with inline style objects on the app-level wrapper elements\n  in all 5 screens (library components imported from\n  @drakkar.software/seahorse are unaffected — they use\n  react-native-css/components directly, a separate code path).\n- components.tsx: IconCard''s `icon` prop expects a React.ReactNode\n  element, not a bare lucide-react-native component reference — fixed\n  to pass <Star .../> instead of Star.\n- forms.tsx: ChipSelect/ToggleRow were called with a prop shape that\n  doesn''t match the real FormSection.tsx API (object options instead\n  of string[] + labels record, onChange instead of onToggle) causing\n  a render crash.\n- native.tsx: top-level @expo/ui primitives (Switch, Column, TextInput,\n  Collapsible, Picker, List, FieldGroup) were direct ScrollView\n  siblings, each self-hosting its own native Host bridge; their\n  independent async size-reporting raced and rendered overlapping.\n  Wrapped everything in one shared <Column> so it collapses into a\n  single Host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b7f343d577ba450cd72b80800be4df4e36266db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Drakkar-Software/SeaHorse/git/trees/7b7f343d577ba450cd72b80800be4df4e36266db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Drakkar-Software/SeaHorse/git/commits/872398c2c8081959537243ebf7c661428c83be04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10454670?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Herklos/events{/privacy